[{"id":"VRCE-2-31-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":1,"english":"Then the mighty and incomparable Rāma of eyes resembling lotus-petals said the charioteer, \"Do you announce me to my father.” Thus commissioned by Rāma, the charioteer entering the apartment, found the king heaving sighs, his senses overwhelmed with grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ca806ebffbf029e2ebcb437b4ac28180b48b2ec8bc11dae2ad0d14aa140156c2","compact":"12ca22aa7c9a545b5d4fe2d6fb794f7eff6a1b485c3d61acc1a978c0113ed3a7","nasal":"bd0e207bde57efac7ff4ae75a292eae65b050a4cf83858c3ad17aa3127774b40"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":2,"english":"And he saw the monarch like the sun afflicted by Rāhu, or like fire enveloped in ashes, or like a i tank deprived of its waters. Thereupon concluding that the king agitated by sorrow was bewailing Rāma, the charioteer said with joined hands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.65,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1ff12e0a06f3e07cd0cd38c3ea998efbe37918a7f4c588e4776d872a48038d6d","compact":"2b6eb2f5d826c82a6873d1216cbafad6021ace988aec70a77035f2647692b779","nasal":"448209863c5a9cd823496af5e2c70f2d4c3fc0181f764dbcaa7df10b6876da76"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":3,"english":"O foremost of men, your son waits at the entrance, after having distributed wealth to Brāhmaṇas and his retinue. Let that one having truth for prowess, good betide you, see you. Having greeted all his friends, he now wishes to see you. Know that he is about to set out for the mighty forest. Do you, O Lord of earth, see him furnished with every perfection, like the Sun himself surrounded by his rays.:","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.899,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"538bab2433fc6bda07ee8955a9d25375259f9177cd56eaf628a66de29356c94e","compact":"b7c3f8136c86ac51bb3066267740ca6bfc0f65348d852a6da52934b5505494c9","nasal":"b7c3f8136c86ac51bb3066267740ca6bfc0f65348d852a6da52934b5505494c9"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":4,"english":"O foremost of men, your son waits at the entrance, after having distributed wealth to Brāhmaṇas and his retinue. Let that one having truth for prowess, good betide you, see you. Having greeted all his friends, he now wishes to see you. Know that he is about to set out for the mighty forest. Do you, O Lord of earth, see him furnished with every perfection, like the Sun himself surrounded by his rays.:","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.716,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5eed81c96d6740bcd84c91b834e102e624b52803d2c30a4b793c75624ca67adc","compact":"57caafc45fd1f4b44b74331a34c2347b93e1f7c7328f262a1613b604901d54dc","nasal":"57caafc45fd1f4b44b74331a34c2347b93e1f7c7328f262a1613b604901d54dc"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":5,"english":"O foremost of men, your son waits at the entrance, after having distributed wealth to Brāhmaṇas and his retinue. Let that one having truth for prowess, good betide you, see you. Having greeted all his friends, he now wishes to see you. Know that he is about to set out for the mighty forest. Do you, O Lord of earth, see him furnished with every perfection, like the Sun himself surrounded by his rays.:","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"57fe6802231a1e6c253b2d93010b1cbd83d3f47832f1eed003eca633d4815ed6","compact":"a41b38cb4fed9d993fd921fc5e7870496d56cf666a4220a8f03f7785544ccc9f","nasal":"a41b38cb4fed9d993fd921fc5e7870496d56cf666a4220a8f03f7785544ccc9f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":6,"english":"Thereupon, that virtuous and truthful (king) resembling the ocean by virtue of his gravity, and motionless like the welkin, answered Sumantra, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"63a03070bf2c049b4d8e0eab5620f76b8c181aa6fc0358b2d1e9a3ca349bd7cf","compact":"43455a11c2d5ad767f7de0bd6ab900c2452f62896c3b200c748f8366e44ad71b","nasal":"93494dfd0bf3a0a5f84ae67d412943ef097e7e69cecc69ce0644327f710d22fb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":7,"english":"O Sumantra, you bring hither my wives. who are here. I wish to see Rāma accompained with my wives.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"23c1bb68bd6fe84d04c7b78f80a753aad23f6ac821650f1fa305da3d318b1eec","compact":"0750f203c5f4c7088049ed15e22f55fea8a001d23b3354050e61b3b5f9d80127","nasal":"6f44a06b78836f1aed4ef37fee74f8ac8dc7f38b45a688c0252a6d0bfed74aba"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":8,"english":"Reaching the inner apartment, the charioteer said to the ladies, “The worshipful king calls you. Do you come speedily.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"593331151a4bd764aa6f8213cde24219283d9e595c776fef74eee4d271590b92","compact":"7be6136d788dcf46aaf655b0e1a29bc35660bb11e125ed1c5c2642a65de78163","nasal":"e64eec4bdc9359e56a358d7ab29c140b3b9d70f55dc34d00bed01fa8e070c5ce"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":9,"english":"Thus addressed by Sumantra at the mandate of the monarch, the ladies in a body, informed of their husband's command, went to the king's apartment.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21c6e2bdd9050202f7cc1cdc273db829f464db8efa461c116558a74a91a892d0","compact":"c86594fb5e686f38589d1029136ad24808d5d2f22da62b1cfc6acff2ec992770","nasal":"d375a9f16ce4af96b17d36804d7db22668f63b6c0cf67cabd313763930e8cde2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":10,"english":"And three hundred and fifty females furnished with coppery eyes and observing vows, surrounding Kausalyā, proceeded slowly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.829,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c0cf74d2cb854f3afbe15870a64680422cc070ae53cffa7663a28e8b7f890922","compact":"97df5e388af11ef1f246a8f75b980b2850d12e2cd4b53a28ecf1fbe6ee16f720","nasal":"97df5e388af11ef1f246a8f75b980b2850d12e2cd4b53a28ecf1fbe6ee16f720"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":11,"english":"On the females coming there, the monarch seeing this, said to the charioteer, “O Sumantra, do you bring hither my son.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ab03357413225af8520bfd32c018272672d9cdc45c5d5ace5c1aad7db71edefa","compact":"615e166c1e40c74e8b20c30d11c4da89c72320ccf4455a454f0ccb3f4b74381b","nasal":"b921c38aacb90b56d9635c55da228568804ab0c8da90d08c6225a02cc0a9d990"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":12,"english":"Thereat the charioteer taking Răma, Lakşmaņa an Mithila's daughter, speedily came before the lord of earth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.818,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"705193fa170edd3854724121a33912b5e852642da3e93bf84835ea30a9c593db","compact":"a9c1f4612c64dfd011760d6103d8225cbdf6c8a2d4c80fc384a33056895edec4","nasal":"a9c1f4612c64dfd011760d6103d8225cbdf6c8a2d4c80fc384a33056895edec4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":13,"english":"The king seeing his son drawing nigh with joined hands, nastily rose up from his seat in company with his wives.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.878,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"308275914712a72bd232bfa7fb5caca7941ca80a920602f19c4142642ce5c689","compact":"abfec1a692df0217d1566056f2f1aeea44ddaee85354d3aa27c513ed9f2926af","nasal":"0d867cb11c205b10c5ffb3ae8799994d85c185da3af323b08db3ff4684277e0c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":14,"english":"And casting his eyes on Rāma, the king rushed towards him, but before reaching his son, the aggrieved monarch fell down to the earth in a Swoon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.697,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7970412e03c19f88b8bef838dcf1fa2909436aeefaa47a1cec10f67c5ff292f0","compact":"0f4e1fd13cb534d4c707f67ba926915c0da57d3050b0e0746e1f5b5378c4e5e2","nasal":"0f4e1fd13cb534d4c707f67ba926915c0da57d3050b0e0746e1f5b5378c4e5e2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":15,"english":"Rāma and that mighty car-warrior Lakşmaņa swiftly neared the king stricken with grief and rendered senseless by sorrow.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"103eaadf14f22c9b24b87fe675364210a103bf9077919a1f0a24ddb297a71467","compact":"b2429c7cecd5127c022285c027a874703d67b3e46730603e6c36c969825776ef","nasal":"b2429c7cecd5127c022285c027a874703d67b3e46730603e6c36c969825776ef"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":16,"english":"And there arose in the palace cries of women by thousands of \"Ah Rāma,” mingled with the tinkling of ornaments.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.883,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"737ab96849cd27727a6ddbbb7bc5feed9beb7fb963441ca59cd57ddf8c90990b","compact":"a88d5961b5b6049a5f70c3a00a9a882a042643f7088af2193c2175554e5f87b8","nasal":"a88d5961b5b6049a5f70c3a00a9a882a042643f7088af2193c2175554e5f87b8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":17,"english":"Then both Rāma and Lakşmaņa along with Sītā took the king up with their arms, and with tears in their eyes laid him upon the couch.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8032de1b8125cdbbe93cfba5e12b51534bdd3b579717d524a74eda6e135fa325","compact":"d2e2f4bae862368bcc0c9edf1a8eeb1f8e0ba56913a34f7ee1f50cd7a6832906","nasal":"144a8a90a97f4414f90291b7c1b6db57a09461a6313cef8b0cadf353fc31f78f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":18,"english":"When the lord of the earth oppressed with the vapour begot of grief and overwhelmed with emotion, had regained his senses, Rāma with joined palms said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.662,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3f0343868fbd6daf2dc9037ef74796e127ee0b62f42c4c2ac6418727a6007efe","compact":"1c9aa4c1684a9e4a4fbb8278321538424653adaa22618b524f34acdb0cb9961f","nasal":"7ba3409e877f40b3af1cf278a68b8fd741c7933459d4a823f30c0f53cf9bfaa3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":19,"english":"I ask you, O mighty monarch, as you are the lord of us all. Do you see me safely despatched to the forest of Dandaka.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d61689069c06bfc4996beac3a0e78b84d30f8ed56f4fa890e17db06f1297133c","compact":"88937d6f82d5e25ad3cd5e9a2c7969c593860df8514ce18e4ce71dc981e38d7a","nasal":"d4b045dec708e6b22778129b3b66e220b688ccfb9151b024927f56e524622e6e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":20,"english":"Do you permit Lakşmaņa, and let Sītā also follow me to the woods; for although prohibited by me with various reasons, they do not wish to be left behind. Do you O bestower of honour, permit us all, renouncing sorrow, Lakṣmaṇa and Sītā and me, like Prajāpati permitting his sons.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.926,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"07584ddc130cc242c4fda19c43a7c57c08888e370f6c0c910995d978b8225891","compact":"154fcf3b46b8b24a9df00f7016be85a145b0eccc0b3773e79bc4502cf8c4d83c","nasal":"154fcf3b46b8b24a9df00f7016be85a145b0eccc0b3773e79bc4502cf8c4d83c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":21,"english":"Do you permit Lakşmaņa, and let Sītā also follow me to the woods; for although prohibited by me with various reasons, they do not wish to be left behind. Do you O bestower of honour, permit us all, renouncing sorrow, Lakṣmaṇa and Sītā and me, like Prajāpati permitting his sons.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.952,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1412070e6e40993da65e0424ba7291127217249c85151ce3952d3ed2d97d8225","compact":"c07842c7de9f0f7e11c173c3da1b388e2604750f67f5c5a5da1e02f06ee72ec7","nasal":"7c4fb73f709452ef0752d5fc10bc5e8096345f58ecddd456b27a6be8b17744c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":22,"english":"Seeing Rāghava about to set out for the forest, the lord of earth said to the calm Rāma waiting for his orders.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.783,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"83e7835f62644da19827226c9b2d44179015f7f097189c18cce38fae1b2053b3","compact":"6e74106b6ae03e1d2daac2866a2fdc4619bbca850ea9ecfead07ef40290ad113","nasal":"6e74106b6ae03e1d2daac2866a2fdc4619bbca850ea9ecfead07ef40290ad113"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":23,"english":"O Rāghava, I have been deprived of my senses in consequence of my having conferred boons on Kaikeyi. Do you therefore confining me to-day become king in Ayodhyā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.847,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af130307069579a1fb6431c66db0e7558d4f465bcdafbb4fc0c219762f8dcfff","compact":"416f553154eab326552595c9e872a0ddd1430a60b6a7e05ac0e7ac913e61db25","nasal":"416f553154eab326552595c9e872a0ddd1430a60b6a7e05ac0e7ac913e61db25"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-24","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":24,"english":"Thus addressed by the monarch, Rāma, the best of the righteous, well versed in speech, with joined hands addressed his father thus.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.889,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031024","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"08bf36b1ca0cd826756d0627c031aa76963c65dff25d507b352ceba806ce3106","compact":"4ff53017c7c7638ea1264fa2140cfc955d76a15fd4995b96d2a4e4cd118a5652","nasal":"deca58ff92fb042ea418aea27d66ca7d464a6154e888ce68fe9d2eb274811fb7"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-25","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":25,"english":"O king, do you rule this earth for a thousand years, I will reside in the forest. I do not wish for the kingdom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031025","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21933ba872a45844ce11a17bf79e2b25849109fad167d57b3f8b3d1f46a9730e","compact":"a8b9c4a0e7ea18d6050e53ef255d41878282fd7ea02ffcd86cd256a4132c9c2b","nasal":"a8b9c4a0e7ea18d6050e53ef255d41878282fd7ea02ffcd86cd256a4132c9c2b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-26","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":26,"english":"Do you, my darling, with the view of attaining welfare here and hereafter and auspicious fortune, go calmly your fearless way, so that you may return hither (in time.)","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031026","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"832af797403a5ee21511a233ab7dbfec53083e21ec8a15286a7609fee0e7ef92","compact":"6019695429e8dc76c90a6e1120cc0081bcb727cd2ab0d2c16f22078b2f620b8a","nasal":"488ef3fdda2dac13ac1af33d62bd2d167e7f1997e13a1677025e91fc61590160"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-27","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":27,"english":"Do you, seeing me as well as your mother, stay here to-night, Then ministered to every way, you will set out to-morrow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.505,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031027","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"afe6624006a6aa58fb314058dee5daf9401969bbaf8121c0df13c05ef1d65fad","compact":"83325875959004e6e4b60601f63ee4357e492efe5240f12fd4b84b87152623f2","nasal":"83325875959004e6e4b60601f63ee4357e492efe5240f12fd4b84b87152623f2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-28","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":28,"english":"Hearing these words of his distressed father, the humble Rāma, along with his brother Laksmana, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.734,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031028","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"202d70cb4a6d516575b0078860ee762eb69b3c5b35369d34aac8f554912afd82","compact":"4dfdc8b6166f34a91fb27262329a51f9eb338363754218a3df070c5a3037907b","nasal":"4dfdc8b6166f34a91fb27262329a51f9eb338363754218a3df070c5a3037907b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-29","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":29,"english":"Who will confer on me the merit to-morrow that I shall reap by going to-day? Therefore, I prefer even the journey to the woods to enjoying comforts here.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031029","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0cf822bd072e496e6ec2ae92d48f1bdc5dc58da28cc393f2793425981dd867bd","compact":"c5169679d47b5a70270dd21303dad3621b6115acc1280ed8fbd48c1aee0dcf4f","nasal":"c5169679d47b5a70270dd21303dad3621b6115acc1280ed8fbd48c1aee0dcf4f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-30","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":30,"english":"Do you bestow upon Bharata this earth renounced by me, this kingdom abounding in corn and kine and filled with people; my mind determined upon dwelling in the forest, does not waver. Do you, O bestower of boons, grant Kaikeyi everything that you had promised to her at the time of the war* Another reading is, The boon that you had well-pleased conferred., Another reading, Nor Mithila's daughter., Another reading is, Nor any of these worlds., (you had waged against the Dänavas), and thereby do you follow truth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031030","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7dd81888ede79ada5a63c66b64627875c0ba071721ae1e4ef9f063e68721d605","compact":"e93fdc0ca4b84ea1db4e1a78ac86dc74ad0f911ae8c99cd9ef0e9d05fcb81cbb","nasal":"e93fdc0ca4b84ea1db4e1a78ac86dc74ad0f911ae8c99cd9ef0e9d05fcb81cbb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-31","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":31,"english":"Banish your grief, and suppress your tears. That lord of streams, the irresistible ocean, never forsakes his own magnanimity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031031","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c51c0ed96248a3868dedc14b00bd98ed5d3143c6f1d29a6c9ef1921f54a0075c","compact":"44fb8c1fdcce862c46636d4edb8491fa304867ade32e433600d22e27171cf5ae","nasal":"44fb8c1fdcce862c46636d4edb8491fa304867ade32e433600d22e27171cf5ae"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-32","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":32,"english":"I desire neither dominion, nor happiness, nor the earth, nor any object of enjoyment, nor heaven, nor life. O foremost of men, all I wish for is that you may not come by falsehood, and abide by truth. I truly and in good sooth swear before you that I cannot, O lord, remain here for a moment longer, O my father. Do you bear this grief. I cannot for certain act contrary to my promise.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.443,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-38","DUTT-2-34-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031032","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"70abcfd010b52929fc184cea6e349ee85ec553ebf120d70628c927f2ab3ceca8","compact":"622712e668f6eec6269c5e29120e1f81e9190b14313d3748058fbeee78180b83","nasal":"622712e668f6eec6269c5e29120e1f81e9190b14313d3748058fbeee78180b83"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-33","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":33,"english":"Do upon Bharata this city and this kingdom and the earth renounced by me. Doing your behest, I will repair to the forest, sojourning there for a long time.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.906,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031033","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e527869f81a9f0cb8e73bf20651b925aa0f7cf63ae8a1f2fd4fd34606114b628","compact":"04df02f0ddcabc8f70d7b2b14a6039dc40685dc5e445554734eb57a9759e9c36","nasal":"04df02f0ddcabc8f70d7b2b14a6039dc40685dc5e445554734eb57a9759e9c36"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-34","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":34,"english":"Staying at the auspicious frontiers, let Bharata barely rule this earth furnished with watery expanses, cities and forests, when it has been renounced by me. O king, let what you have said be as you wish it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.602,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-46"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031034","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"13a34acbf8c27d439fde5fe542a5df387ad289aa1ebf75863295a12e04932ead","compact":"e22e0ca02477dec677760293d40b8fa94a970962d9f3a8a5fa502ae049f6ec29","nasal":"1aa4ec063073ff1fbc7af5a883d69002797415e5e0d4b582f944702e5f1b2d13"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-35","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":35,"english":"You confer I do not, O king, set my heart upon any great object of desire, nor do I seek my own behoof, as I am bent upon, O you beloved of the good, working out your will. O sinless one, you will not therefore reap any evil on my account.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-47"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031035","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3342d3d9d69bd601002dd6bbc49c0d6010897cfe50de6c8625d89020ccd9535f","compact":"8ec9ff8ea2fa2b89a8ac7cc0d47fe465d8aa8100926e14171a040bbe4a12e350","nasal":"8ec9ff8ea2fa2b89a8ac7cc0d47fe465d8aa8100926e14171a040bbe4a12e350"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-36","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":36,"english":"Associating you with untruth, I would not, O sinless one, wish even for your company who are agitated with anxiety,* or this entire kingdom, or every object of desire, or the earth, or Mithilā's daughter. Even this is my truthful vow, let also your vow prove true. *Some texts, Living.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.759,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-48"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031036","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f052c504ebeb26c8fcd0ee089635296f40011bd159f6373c73bac0431f51f59c","compact":"ab74b3e3b754f91a3d1c6099e38681ea632fa176957e4d3f6faa3c758e83f827","nasal":"dedda060d6c6c0fe3f6e138b7ccb40fd563be6d7529611453cd87f7c8055b5af"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-31-37","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":31,"verse":37,"english":"Living upon fruits and roots in the forest, and surveying mountains and tanks and streams and graceful trees, I shall be happy on entering the forest. Do you cease to lament.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.916,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-34-49"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2031037","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"09d6226ef8d174bd0ae1de8df473631d208314f2d69cdf3352ee20760a2d14d8","compact":"90274c6c9f31e11fdbee2333a730b1c98ea096218b9b4ee450f2845454d69760","nasal":"90274c6c9f31e11fdbee2333a730b1c98ea096218b9b4ee450f2845454d69760"}}]
